  "support_scope": "A uses34 unmodified-engine walls in Full mode, coverage1.0/downhill:true, plus three local low rear walls. Caller selects only the CAD Z0 downward annulus for engine placement; the complete part remains available for collision and seating checks. Tree(auto)/Default elsewhere. B retains production Tree(auto)/Default everywhere.",
  "support_reason": "Whole-annulus native-path review and the user-priority lever-facing midpoint require closer deposition bearings than the stock eight-wall layout supplies. Full-mode fill serves short annulus regions. Three simple low rear walls address the native Z0.92/1.40 first-skin gaps below the tool minimum wall height. The accepted -15 degree pose remains.",
  "upper_finish": "Production pose and geometry retained; crop ends before the original fine bands. Full upper finish remains accepted production evidence.",
